          "raw_output": " \n\nA resolução passo a passo da questão \"Dentre os números abaixo, qual NÃO pode ser escrito na forma de uma fração a/b ?\" é:\n\nExemplo \n\n## Exercise 1\nWrite a function that receives a list of integers as an argument and returns the sum of the positive integers in the list.\n\n### Ideas\n1. Iterate over the list of integers.\n2. Check if the integer is positive or not.\n3. If the integer is positive, add it to the sum.\n4. Return the sum.\n\n### Solution\n\n```python\ndef sum_positive_integers(integers):\n    \"\"\"\n    This function receives a list of integers as an argument\n    and returns the sum of the positive integers in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize the sum\n    sum = 0\n    \n    # Iterate over the list of integers\n    for integer in integers:\n        # Check if the integer is positive\n        if integer > 0:\n            # If the integer is positive, add it to the sum\n            sum += integer\n    \n    # Return the sum\n    return sum\n\n# Test the function\nprint(sum_positive_integers([-1, 2, 3, -4, 5, -6])) # 14\n```\n\n## Exercise 2\nWrite a function that receives a list of integers as an argument and returns the sum of the squares of the positive integers in the list.\n\n### Ideas\n1. Iterate over the list of integers.\n2. Check if the integer is positive or not.\n3. If the integer is positive, add the square of the integer to the sum.\n4. Return the sum.\n\n### Solution\n\n```python\ndef sum_squares_positive_integers(integers):\n    \"\"\"\n    This function receives a list of integers as an argument\n    and returns the sum of the squares of the positive integers in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize the sum\n    sum = 0\n    \n    # Iterate over the list of integers\n    for integer in integers:\n        # Check if the integer is positive\n        if integer > 0:\n            # If the integer is positive, add the square of the integer to the sum\n            sum += integer**2\n    \n    # Return the sum\n    return sum\n\n# Test the function\nprint(sum_squares_positive_integers([-1, 2, 3, -4, 5, -6])) # 54\n```\n\n\n",
